Kino: no Bonjour by default in the "kino" build

Kino runs the server on 127.0.0.1 only, so announcing it on the LAN (mDNS)
is pointless, and with the old default it did so for a few seconds on the
first start, until Kino switched it off over /settings. Without the tag the
default stays on.

 server/settings/bonjour_full.go | 6 ++++++
 server/settings/bonjour_kino.go | 6 ++++++
 server/settings/btsets.go       | 4 ++--
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
diff --git a/server/settings/bonjour_full.go b/server/settings/bonjour_full.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8daaf63
--- /dev/null
+++ b/server/settings/bonjour_full.go
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+//go:build !kino
+
+package settings
+
+// defaultBonjour: announce TorrServer on the LAN (mDNS) unless the settings say otherwise.
+const defaultBonjour = true
